#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:58
msgid ""
"This RFC builds on a large collection of prior art collated in the [`build-"
"std-context`](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3873-build-std-context."
"html#proposal) RFC, and is aimed at supporting the following [motivations]"
"(https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3873-build-std-context.html#motivation) it "
"identifies:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:62
msgid ""
"Building the standard library without relying on unstable escape hatches"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:63
msgid "Building standard library crates that are not shipped for a target"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:64
msgid "Using the standard library with tier three targets"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:66
msgid ""
"While the enabling and disabling of some standard library features is "
"mentioned in this RFC (when required to support existing stable features of "
"Cargo), the enabling and disabling of arbitrary standard library features is "
"handled by [RFC #3875](https://github.com/davidtwco/rfcs/blob/build-std-part-"
"three-explicit-dependencies/text/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies."
"md#features)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:71
msgid ""
"A key goal of this proposal is that the standard library produced by `build-"
"std.when = \"always\"` be a drop-in replacement for the pre-build standard "
"library, so that the new surface area of the standard library exposed by "
"build-std is minimal (while providing extension points for this to be "
"changed in future in limited and controlled ways)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:79
msgid "Proposal"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:82
msgid ""
"This proposal section is quite broad, and a [summary of changes](#summary-of-"
"proposed-changes) is available for a very brief list of proposed changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:86
msgid ""
"Cargo configuration will contain a new table `build-std` under the `[build]` "
"section ([?](#why-put-build-std-in-the-cargo-config)), with a `when` key "
"permitting one of two values - \"never\" ([?](#why-accept-never-as-a-value-"
"for-build-std)) or \"always\", defaulting to \"never\":"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:91
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[build]\n"
"build-std.when = \"never\" # or `always`\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:96
msgid ""
"`build-std` can also be specified in the `[target.<triple>]` and `[target."
"<cfg>]` sections ([?](#why-add-build-std-to-the-targettriple-and-targetcfg-"
"sections)):"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:99
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[target.aarch64-unknown-illumos]\n"
"build-std.when = \"never\" # or `always`\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:104
msgid ""
"The `build-std` configuration locations have the following precedence ([?]"
"(#why-does-target-take-precedence-over-build-for-build-std)):"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:107
msgid "`[target.<triple>]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:108
msgid "`[target.<cfg>]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:109
msgid "`[build]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:111
msgid ""
"As the Cargo configuration is local to the current user (typically in `."
"config/cargo.toml` in the project root and/or Cargo home directory), the "
"value of `build-std` is not influenced by the dependencies of the current "
"crate."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:115
msgid ""
"When `build-std` is set to \"always\", then the standard library will be "
"unconditionally recompiled ([?](#why-have-a-manual-always-option-instead-of-"
"a-when-needed-mode)) in the release profile ([?](#why-does-always-rebuild-in-"
"release-profile)) defined in its workspace as part of every clean build. "
"This is primarily useful for users of tier three targets."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:120
msgid ""
"As with other dependencies, the standard library's build will respect the "
"`RUSTFLAGS` environment variable. `RUSTFLAGS` is respected irrespective of "
"the mechanism that it is set via: `RUSTFLAGS`, `CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS`, "
"`target.<triple>.rustflags` or `target.<cfg>.rustflags`. The unstable "
"`profile.rustflags` key is also respected, but from the same profile as the "
"rest of the standard library build (i.e. it uses the release profile of the "
"standard library's workspace)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:128 src/3874-build-std-always.md:165
#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:362 src/3874-build-std-always.md:395
#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:421 src/3874-build-std-always.md:483
#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:652 src/3874-build-std-always.md:1643
msgid "\\[!NOTE\\]"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:130
msgid ""
"Configuration of the pre-built standard library is split across bootstrap "
"and the Cargo packages for the standard library. As much of this "
"configuration as possible should be moved to the Cargo profile for these "
"packages so that the artifacts produced by build-std match the pre-built "
"standard library as much as is feasible."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:136
msgid ""
"Alongside `build-std`, a `build-std.crates` key will be introduced ([?](#why-"
"add-build-stdcrates)), which can be used to specify which crates from the "
"standard library should be built. Only \"core\", \"alloc\" and \"std\" are "
"valid values for `build-std.crates`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:141
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[build]\n"
"build-std = { when = \"always\", crates = \"std\" }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:146
msgid ""
"A value of \"std\" means that every crate in the graph has a direct "
"dependency on `std`, `alloc` and `core`. Similarly, \"alloc\" means `alloc` "
"and `core`, and \"core\" means just `core`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:150
msgid ""
"If `std` is to be built and Cargo is building a test or benchmark using the "
"default test harness then Cargo will also build the `test` crate."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:153
msgid ""
"When `build-std.crates` is unset, then the standard library crates built "
"will depend on whether [_Standard library dependencies_](https://github.com/"
"rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3875) are implemented:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:156
msgid ""
"If [_Standard library dependencies_](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/"
"pull/3875) _is not_ implemented, then the crates intended to be supported by "
"the target inform which crates are built (see later [_Standard library crate "
"stability_](#standard-library-crate-stability) section)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:161
msgid ""
"If [_Standard library dependencies_](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/"
"pull/3875) _is_ implemented, then the implicit or explicit `builtin` "
"dependencies of the crate graph inform which crates are built ."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:167
msgid ""
"Inspired by the concept of [opaque dependencies](https://github.com/rust-"
"lang/cargo/issues/3573#issuecomment-3498262549), the standard library is "
"resolved differently to other dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:170
msgid ""
"The lockfile included in the standard library source will be used when "
"resolving the standard library's dependencies ([?](#why-use-the-lockfile-of-"
"the-rust-src-component))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:173
msgid ""
"The dependencies of the standard library crates are entirely opaque to the "
"user. Different semver-compatible versions of these dependencies can exist "
"in the user's resolve. The user cannot control compilation any of the "
"dependencies of the `core`, `alloc` or `std` standard library crates "
"individually (via profile overrides, for example)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:179
msgid "The release profile defined by the standard library will be used."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:181
msgid ""
"This profile will be updated to match the current compilation options used "
"by the pre-built standard library as much as possible (e.g. using `-Cembed-"
"bitcode=yes` to support LTO)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:185
msgid ""
"Standard library crates and their dependencies from `build-std.crates` "
"cannot be patched/replaced by the user in the Cargo manifest or config (e.g. "
"using source replacement, `[replace]` or `[patch]`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:189
msgid ""
"Lints in standard library crates will be built using `--cap-lints allow` "
"matching other upstream dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:192
msgid ""
"Cargo will resolve the dependencies of opaque dependencies, such as the "
"standard library, separately in their own workspaces. The root of such a "
"resolve will be the crates specified in `build-std.crates` or, if [_Standard "
"library dependencies_](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3875) is "
"implemented, the unified set of packages that any crate in the dependency "
"has a direct dependency on. A dependency on the relevant roots are added to "
"all crates in the main resolve."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:199
msgid ""
"Regardless of which standard library crates are being built, Cargo will "
"build the `sysroot` crate of the standard library workspace. `alloc` and "
"`std` will be optional dependencies of the `sysroot` crate which will be "
"enabled when the user has requested them. Panic runtimes are dependencies of "
"`std` and will be enabled depending on the features that Cargo passes to "
"`std` (see [_Panic strategies_](#panic-strategies))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:206
msgid ""
"rustc loads panic runtimes in a different way to most dependencies, and "
"without looking in the sysroot they will fail to load correctly unless "
"passed in with `--extern`. rustc will need to be patched to be able to load "
"panic runtimes from `-L dependency=` paths in line with other transitive "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:212
msgid ""
"The standard library will always be a non-incremental build ([?](#why-not-"
"build-the-standard-library-in-incremental)), Cargo's dep-info fingerprint "
"tracking will not track the standard library crate sources, Cargo's `.d` dep-"
"info file will not include standard library crate sources, and only a `rlib` "
"produced (no `dylib`) ([?](#why-not-produce-a-dylib-for-the-standard-"
"library)). It will be built in the Cargo `target` directory of the crate or "
"workspace like any other dependency. The `rlib`s of the standard library are "
"considered intermediate artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:220
msgid ""
"Standard library crates are provided to the compiler using the `--extern` "
"flag with the `noprelude` modifier ([?](#why-use-noprelude-with---extern)). "
"Standard library crates are also provided with the `nounused` modifier to "
"avoid being considered an unused crate dependency ([?](#why-use-nounused-"
"with---extern))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:225
msgid ""
"The host pre-built standard library will always be used for procedural "
"macros and build scripts ([?](#why-use-the-pre-built-standard-library-for-"
"procedural-macros-and-build-scripts-in-cross-compile-mode), [?](#why-use-the-"
"pre-built-standard-library-for-procedural-macros-and-build-scripts-in-host-"
"mode)). Multi-target projects (resulting from the `target` field in artifact "
"dependencies or the use of `per-pkg-target` fields) may result in the "
"standard library being built multiple times - once for each target in the "
"project."
msgstr ""

