#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:262
msgid "Standard library crate stability"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:265
msgid ""
"An optional `standard_library_support` field ([?](#why-introduce-"
"standard_library_support)) is added to the target specification ([?](#should-"
"target-specifications-own-knowledge-of-which-standard-library-crates-are-"
"supported)), replacing the existing `metadata.std` field. "
"`standard_library_support` has two fields:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:270
msgid ""
"`supported`, which can be set to either \"core\", \"core, alloc\", or "
"\"core, alloc, std\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:272
msgid ""
"`default`, which can be set to either \"core\", \"core, alloc\", or \"core, "
"alloc, std\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:274
msgid ""
"`default` cannot be set to a value which is \"less than\" that of "
"`supported` (i.e. \"core, alloc\" when `supported` was only set to \"core\")"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:277
msgid ""
"The `supported` field determines which standard library crates Cargo will "
"permit to be built for this target on a stable toolchain. On a nightly "
"toolchain, Cargo will build whichever standard library crates are requested "
"by the user."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:281
msgid ""
"The `default` field determines which crate will be built by Cargo if `build-"
"std.when = \"always\"` and `build-std.crates` is not set. Users can specify "
"`build-std.crates` to build more crates than included in the `default`, as "
"long as those crates are included in `supported`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:286
msgid ""
"The correct value for `standard_library_support` is independent of the tier "
"of the target and depends on the set of crates that are intended to work for "
"a given target, according to its maintainers."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:290
msgid ""
"If `standard_library_support` is unset for a target, then Cargo will not "
"permit any standard library crates to be built for the target on a stable "
"toolchain. It will be required to use a nightly toolchain to use build-std "
"with that target."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:294
msgid ""
"Cargo's `build-std.crates` field will default to the value of the "
"`standard_library_support.default` field (`std` for \"core, alloc, std\", "
"`alloc` for \"core, alloc\", and `core` for \"core\"). This does not prevent "
"users from building more crates than the default, it is only intended to be "
"a sensible default for the target that is probably what the user expects."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:300
msgid ""
"The `target-standard-library-support` option will be supported by rustc's `--"
"print` flag and will be used by Cargo to query this value for a given target:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:312
msgid ""
"Following [compiler-team#860](https://github.com/rust-lang/compiler-team/"
"issues/860), `target-standard-library-support` can also be output in JSON:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:315
msgid ""
"```shell-session\n"
"$ rustc --print target-standard-library-support:json --target armv7a-none-"
"eabi\n"
"{ \"default\": \"core\", \"supported\": [\"core\", \"alloc\"] }\n"
"$ rustc --print target-standard-library-support:json --target aarch64-"
"unknown-linux-gnu\n"
"{ \"default\": \"core\", \"supported\": [\"core\", \"alloc\", \"std\"] }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:324
msgid ""
"[_Why introduce `standard_library_support`?_](#why-introduce-"
"standard_library_support)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:325
msgid ""
"[_Should target specifications own knowledge of which standard library "
"crates are supported?_](#should-target-specifications-own-knowledge-of-which-"
"standard-library-crates-are-supported)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:329
msgid "Interactions with `#![no_std]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:332
msgid ""
"Behaviour of crates using `#![no_std]` will not change whether or not `std` "
"is rebuilt and passed via `--extern` to rustc, and `#![no_std]` will still "
"be required in order for `rustc` to not attempt to load `std` and add it to "
"the extern prelude. [_Standard library dependencies_](https://github.com/"
"rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3875) describes a future possibility for how the "
"`no_std` mechanism could be replaced."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:340
msgid ""
"[_Replace `#![no_std]` as the source-of-truth for whether a crate depends on "
"`std`_](https://github.com/davidtwco/rfcs/blob/build-std-part-three-explicit-"
"dependencies/text/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md#replace-no_std-as-"
"the-source-of-truth-for-whether-a-crate-depends-on-std) (RFC 3875)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:344
msgid "`restricted_std`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:347
msgid ""
"The existing `restricted_std` mechanism will be removed from `std`'s [`build."
"rs`](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/"
"f315e6145802e091ff9fceab6db627a4b4ec2b86/library/std/build.rs#L17)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:352
msgid "[_Why remove `restricted_std`?_](#why-remove-restricted_std)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:356
msgid "Custom targets"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:359
msgid ""
"Cargo will detect when the standard library is to be built for a custom "
"target and will emit an error ([?](#why-disallow-custom-targets))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:364
msgid ""
"Cargo could detect use of a custom target either by comparing it with the "
"list of built-in targets that rustc reports knowing about (via `--print "
"target-list`) or by checking if a file exists at the path matching the "
"provided target name."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:368
msgid ""
"This does not require any changes to rustc. If it is invoked to build the "
"standard library then it will continue to do so, as is possible today, it is "
"only the build-std functionality in Cargo that will not support custom "
"targets initially."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:373
msgid ""
"Furthermore, custom targets will be destabilised in rustc (as in [rust#71009]"
"(https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/71009)). This will not be a "
"significant breaking change as custom targets cannot effectively be used "
"currently without nightly (needing build-std to have `core`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:378
msgid ""
"Custom targets can still be used with build-std on nightly toolchains "
"provided that `-Zunstable-options` is provided to Cargo."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:383
msgid "[_Why disallow custom targets?_](#why-disallow-custom-targets)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:387
msgid ""
"[_Allow custom targets with build-std_](#allow-custom-targets-with-build-std)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:389
msgid "Preventing implicit sysroot dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:392
msgid ""
"Cargo will pass a new flag to rustc which will prevent rustc from loading "
"top-level dependencies from the sysroot ([?](#why-prevent-rustc-from-loading-"
"root-dependencies-from-the-sysroot))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:397
msgid ""
"rustc could add a `--no-implicit-sysroot-deps` flag with this behaviour. For "
"example, writing `extern crate foo` in a crate will not load `foo.rlib` from "
"the sysroot if it is present, but if an `--extern noprelude:bar.rlib` is "
"provided which depends on a crate `foo`, rustc will look in `-L "
"dependency=...` paths and the sysroot for it."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:405
msgid ""
"[_Why prevent rustc from loading root dependencies from the sysroot?_](#why-"
"prevent-rustc-from-loading-root-dependencies-from-the-sysroot)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:407
msgid "Vendored `rust-src`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:410
msgid ""
"When it is necessary to build the standard library, Cargo will look for "
"sources in a fixed location in the sysroot ([?](#why-not-allow-the-source-"
"path-for-the-standard-library-be-customised)): `lib/rustlib/src`. rustup's "
"`rust-src` component downloads standard library sources to this location and "
"will be made a default component. If the sources are not found, Cargo will "
"emit an error and recommend the user download `rust-src` if using rustup."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:417
msgid ""
"`rust-src` will contain the sources for the standard library crates as well "
"as its vendored dependencies ([?](#why-vendor-the-standard-librarys-"
"dependencies)). As a consequence sources of standard library dependencies "
"will not need be fetched from crates.io."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:423
msgid ""
"Cargo will not perform any checks to ensure that the sources in `rust-src` "
"have been modified ([?](#why-not-check-if-rust-src-has-been-modified)). It "
"will be documented that modifying these sources is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:429
msgid ""
"[_Why not allow the source path for the standard library be customised?_]"
"(#why-not-allow-the-source-path-for-the-standard-library-be-customised)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:430
msgid ""
"[_Why vendor standard library dependencies?_](#why-vendor-the-standard-"
"librarys-dependencies)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:431
msgid ""
"[_Why not check if `rust-src` has been modified?_](#why-not-check-if-rust-"
"src-has-been-modified)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:435
msgid ""
"[_Should `rust-src` be a default component?_](#should-rust-src-be-a-default-"
"component)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:437
msgid "Panic strategies"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:440
msgid ""
"Panic strategies are unlike other profile settings insofar as they influence "
"which crates are built and which flags are passed to the standard library "
"build. For example, if `panic = \"unwind\"` were set in the Cargo profile "
"then the `panic_unwind` feature would need to be provided to `std` and `-"
"Cpanic=unwind` passed to suggest that the compiler use that panic runtime."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:446
msgid ""
"If Cargo is not building `std`, then neither of the panic runtimes will be "
"built. In this circumstance rustc will continue to throw an error when a "
"unwinding panic strategy is chosen."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:450
msgid ""
"If Cargo would build `std` for a project then Cargo's behaviour depends on "
"whether or not `panic` is set in the profile:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:453
msgid ""
"If `panic` is not set in the profile then unwinding may still be the default "
"for the target and Cargo will need to enable the `panic_unwind` feature to "
"the `sysroot` crate to build `panic_unwind` just in case it is used"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:457
msgid ""
"If `panic` is set to \"unwind\" then the `panic_unwind` feature of `sysroot` "
"will be enabled and `-Cpanic=unwind` will be passed"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:460
msgid "If `panic` is set to \"abort\" then `-Cpanic=abort` will be passed"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:462
msgid ""
"`panic_abort` is a non-optional dependency of `std` so it will always be "
"built"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:465
msgid ""
"If `panic` is set to \"immediate-abort\" then `-Cpanic=immediate-abort` will "
"be passed"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:468
msgid ""
"Neither `panic_abort` or `panic_unwind` need to be built, but as "
"`panic_abort` is non-optional, it will be"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:471
msgid "`-Cpanic=immediate-abort` is unstable"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:473
msgid ""
"Tests, benchmarks, build scripts and proc macros continue to ignore the "
"\"panic\" setting and `panic = \"unwind\"` is always used - which means the "
"standard library needs to be recompiled again if the user is using "
"\"abort\". Once `panic-abort-tests` is stabilised, the standard library can "
"be built with the profile's panic strategy even for tests and benchmarks."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:479
msgid ""
"In line with Cargo's stance on not parsing the `RUSTFLAGS` environment "
"variable, it will not be checked for compilation flags that would require "
"additional crates to be built for compilation to succeed."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:485
msgid ""
"The `unwind` crate will continue to link to the system's `libunwind` which "
"will need to match the target modifiers used by the standard library to "
"avoid incompatibilities. Likewise, if `llvm-libunwind`, `-Clink-self-"
"contained=yes` or `-Ctarget-feature=+crt-static` are used and the "
"distributed `libunwind` is used then it will also need to match the target "
"modifiers of the standard library to avoid incompatibilities."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:494
msgid ""
"[_Avoid building `panic_unwind` unnecessarily_](#avoid-building-panic_unwind-"
"unnecessarily)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:496
msgid "Building the standard library on a stable toolchain"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:499
msgid ""
"rustc will automatically assume `RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP` when the source path of "
"the crate being compiled is within the same sysroot as the rustc binary "
"being invoked ([?](#why-allow-building-from-the-sysroot-with-implied-"
"rustc_bootstrap)). Cargo will not need to use `RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP` when "
"compiling the standard library with a stable toolchain. The standard "
"library's dependencies will not be permitted to use build probes to detect "
"whether a nightly version is being used (at time of writing, currently only "
"`object` and `libc` detect the rustc version in their `build.rs`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:509
msgid ""
"[_Why allow building from the sysroot with implied `RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP`?_](#why-"
"allow-building-from-the-sysroot-with-implied-rustc_bootstrap)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:511
msgid "Self-contained objects"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:514
msgid ""
"A handful of targets require linking against special object files, such as "
"`windows-gnu`, `linux-musl` and `wasi` targets. For example, `linux-musl` "
"targets require `crt1.o`, `crti.o`, `crtn.o`, etc."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:518
msgid ""
"Since [rust#76158](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/76158)/[compiler-"
"team#343](https://github.com/rust-lang/compiler-team/issues/343), the "
"compiler has a stable `-Clink-self-contained` flag which will look for "
"special object files in expected locations, typically populated by the `rust-"
"std` components. Its behaviour can be forced by `-Clink-self-"
"contained=true`, but is force-enabled for some targets and inferred for "
"others."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:524
msgid ""
"Rust will ship `rust-self-contained` components for any targets which need "
"it. These components will contain the special object files normally included "
"in `rust-std`, and will be distributed for all tiers of targets. While "
"generally these objects are specific to the architecture and C runtime (CRT) "
"(and so `rust-self-contained-$arch-$crt` could be sufficient and result in "
"fewer overall components), it's technically possible that Rust could support "
"two targets with the same architecture and same CRT but different versions "
"of the CRT, so having target-specific components is most future-proof. These "
"would replace the `self-contained` directory in existing `rust-std` "
"components."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:534
msgid ""
"Similarly, for any architectures which require it, LLVM's `libunwind` will "
"be built and shipped in the `rust-self-contained` component."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:537
msgid ""
"As long as these components have been downloaded, as well as any other "
"support components, such as `rust-mingw`, rustc's `-Clink-self-contained` "
"will be able to link against the object files and build-std should never "
"fail on account of missing special object files. rustc will attempt to "
"detect when `rust-self-contained` components are missing and provide helpful "
"diagnostics in this case."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:544
msgid ""
"`-Clink-self-contained` also controls whether rustc uses the linker shipped "
"with Rust. build-std's use of `-Clink-self-contained` will endeavour to "
"ensure that the whatever the default linker for the current target is (self-"
"contained or otherwise) will be used."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:551
msgid ""
"[_Enable local recompilation of special object files/sanitizer runtimes_]"
"(#enable-local-recompilation-of-special-object-filessanitizer-runtimes)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:556
msgid "`compiler-builtins`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:559
msgid ""
"`compiler-builtins` is always built with `-Ccodegen-units=10000` to force "
"each intrinsic into its own object file to avoid symbol clashes with libgcc. "
"This is currently enforced with a profile override in the standard library's "
"workspace and is unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:564
msgid ""
"See [_Allow local builds of `compiler-rt` intrinsics_](https://github.com/"
"davidtwco/rfcs/blob/build-std-part-three-explicit-dependencies/text/3875-"
"build-std-explicit-dependencies.md#allow-local-builds-of-compiler-rt-"
"intrinsics) for discussion of the `compiler-builtins-c` feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:569
msgid "`compiler-builtins/mem`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:572
msgid ""
"It is not possible to use weak linkage to make the symbols provided by "
"`compiler_builtins/mem` trivially overridable in every case ([?](#why-not-"
"use-weak-linkage-for-compiler-builtinsmem-symbols))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:576
msgid ""
"The `mem` feature of `compiler_builtins` will be inverted to a new feature "
"named `external-mem` ([?](#why-invert-the-mem-feature)). This will not be a "
"default feature, so `compiler_builtins` will provide mem symbols unless the "
"`external-mem` is provided."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:581
msgid ""
"`std`, which provides memory symbols via `libc`, will depend on the "
"`external-mem` feature. Most `no_std` users will use the `compiler_builtins` "
"implementation of these symbols and will work by default when they do not "
"depend on `std`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:586
msgid ""
"Those users providing their own mem symbols can override on weak linkage of "
"the `compiler_builtins` symbols, or use a nightly toolchain to enable the "
"`external-mem` feature of an explicit dependency on the standard library "
"(per [_Standard library dependencies_](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/"
"pull/3875))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:593
msgid ""
"[_Why not rely on weak linkage for `compiler-builtins/mem` symbols?_](#why-"
"not-use-weak-linkage-for-compiler-builtinsmem-symbols)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:594
msgid "[_Why invert the `mem` feature?_](#why-invert-the-mem-feature)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:596
msgid "`profiler-builtins`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:599
msgid ""
"`profiler-builtins` will not be built by build-std, thus preventing profile-"
"guided optimisation with a locally-built standard library. `profiler-"
"builtins` has native dependencies which may fail compilation of the standard "
"library if missing were `profiler-builtins` to be built by default as part "
"of the standard library build."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:607
msgid ""
"[_Allow building `profiler-builtins`_](#allow-building-profiler-builtins)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:609
msgid "Caching"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:612
msgid ""
"Standard library artifacts built by build-std will be reused equivalently to "
"today's crates/dependencies that are built within a shared target directory. "
"By default, this limits sharing to a single workspace ([?](#why-not-globally-"
"cache-builds-of-the-standard-library))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:618
msgid ""
"[_Why not globally cache builds of the standard library?_](#why-not-globally-"
"cache-builds-of-the-standard-library)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:620
msgid "Generated documentation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:623
msgid ""
"When running `cargo doc` for a project to generate documentation and "
"rebuilding the standard library, the generated documentation for the user's "
"crates will link to the locally generated documentation for the `core`, "
"`alloc` and `std` crates, rather than the upstream hosted generation as is "
"typical for non-locally built standard libraries."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:631
msgid ""
"[_Why not link to hosted standard library documentation in generated docs?_]"
"(#why-not-link-to-hosted-standard-library-documentation-in-generated-docs)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:633
msgid "Cargo subcommands"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:636
msgid ""
"Any Cargo command which accepts a package spec with `-p` will not recognise "
"`core`, `alloc`, `std` or none of their dependencies (unless [_Standard "
"library dependencies_](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3875) is "
"implemented). Many of Cargo's subcommands will need modification to support "
"build-std:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:641
msgid ""
"[`cargo clean`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-clean.html) "
"will additionally delete any builds of the standard library performed by "
"build-std. See also [_Should `cargo clean` delete builds of the standard "
"library?_](#should-cargo-clean-delete-builds-of-the-standard-library)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:645
msgid ""
"[`cargo fetch`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-fetch.html) "
"will not fetch the standard library dependencies as they are already "
"vendored in the `rust-src` component."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:648
msgid ""
"[`cargo miri`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-miri.html) is "
"not built into Cargo, it is shipped by miri, but is mentioned in Cargo's "
"documentation. `cargo miri` is unchanged by this RFC, but build-std is one "
"step towards `cargo miri` requiring less special support."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:654
msgid ""
"`cargo miri` could be re-implemented using build-std to enable a `miri` "
"profile and always rebuild. The `miri` profile would be configured in the "
"standard library's workspace, setting the flags/options necessary for `miri`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:658
msgid ""
"[`cargo report`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-report.html) "
"will not include reports from the standard library crates or their "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:661
msgid ""
"[`cargo update`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-update.html) "
"will not update the dependencies of `std`, `alloc` and `core`, as these are "
"vendored as part of the distribution of `rust-src` and resolved separately "
"from the user's dependencies. Neither will `std`, `alloc` or `core` be "
"updated, as these are unversioned and always match the current toolchain "
"version."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:667
msgid ""
"[`cargo vendor`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-vendor.html) "
"will not vendor the standard library crates or their dependencies. These are "
"pre-vendored as part of the `rust-src` component ([?](#why-vendor-the-"
"standard-librarys-dependencies))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:671
msgid ""
"The following commands will now build the standard library if required as "
"part of the compilation of the project, just like any other dependency:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:674
msgid ""
"[`cargo bench`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-bench.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:675
msgid ""
"[`cargo build`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-build.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:676
msgid ""
"[`cargo check`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-check.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:677
msgid ""
"[`cargo clippy`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-clippy.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:678
msgid "[`cargo doc`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-doc.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:679
msgid "[`cargo fix`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-fix.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:680
msgid "[`cargo run`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-run.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:681
msgid ""
"[`cargo rustc`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-rustc.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:682
msgid ""
"[`cargo rustdoc`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-rustdoc."
"html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:683
msgid ""
"[`cargo test`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-test.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:685
msgid ""
"This part of the RFC has no implications for the following Cargo subcommands:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:687
msgid "[`cargo add`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-add.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:688
msgid ""
"[`cargo remove`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-remove.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:689
msgid "[`cargo fmt`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-fmt.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:690
msgid ""
"[`cargo generate-lockfile`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-"
"generate-lockfile.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:691
msgid ""
"[`cargo help`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-help.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:692
msgid ""
"[`cargo info`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-info.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:693
msgid ""
"[`cargo init`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-init.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:694
msgid ""
"[`cargo install`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-install."
"html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:695
msgid ""
"[`cargo locate-project`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-"
"locate-project.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:696
msgid ""
