#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:1612
msgid "New constraints on the standard library, compiler and bootstrap"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:1615
msgid ""
"A stable mechanism for building the standard library imposes some "
"constraints on the rest of the toolchain that would need to be upheld:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:1618
msgid ""
"No further required customisation of the pre-built standard library through "
"any means other than the profile in `Cargo.toml`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:1620
msgid "Avoid mandatory C dependencies on the standard library"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:1621
msgid ""
"At the very least, new dependencies on the standard library will impact "
"whether the standard library can be successfully built by users with varying "
"environments and this impact will need to be considered going forward"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:1624
msgid ""
"New C dependencies will need to be careful not to cause symbol conflicts "
"with user crates that pull in the same dependency (e.g. using [`links =...`]"
"(https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/cargo/reference/manifest.html#the-links-"
"field))"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:1627
msgid ""
"If this did come up, it might be possible to work around it with "
"postprocessing that renames C symbols used by the standard library but that "
"would be better avoided"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:1630
msgid ""
"The standard library continues to exist in its own workspace, with its own "
"lockfile"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:1632
msgid "The name of the `test` crate becomes stable (but not its interface)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:1633
msgid ""
"The `panic-unwind` and `compiler-builtins-mem` `sysroot` features become "
"stable so Cargo can refer to them"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:1635
msgid ""
"This should not necessitate a \"stable/unstable features\" mechanism, rather "
"a guarantee from the library team that they're happy for these to stay"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:1637
msgid ""
"Dependencies of the standard library cannot use build probes to detect "
"whether nightly features can be used"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:1639
msgid ""
"With [_Assuming `RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP` for sysroot builds_](#building-the-"
"standard-library-on-a-stable-toolchain), these build probes would always "
"assume the crate is being built on nightly"
msgstr ""

#: src/3874-build-std-always.md:1645
msgid ""
"Cargo will likely be made a [JOSH](https://josh-project.github.io/josh/intro."
"html) subtree of the [rust-lang/rust](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust) so "
"that all relevant parts of the toolchain can be updated in tandem when this "
"is necessary."
msgstr ""
